/-!
# The abelian-closure branch of Section 15.3

The conditional fusion implications of Lemma 15.3.62 are proved from the
natural orthogonal action and the genuine earlier local conclusions.
A totally singular escaping four-group is constructed from `r(G,V)=2`.
The terminal subgroups, including the temporary normalizer used only
inside the proof of 15.3.67, have their source definitions.

The weak-closure and module bounds 15.3.63–65, the line-normalizer
recognition 15.3.66–67, and the Goldschmidt conclusions 15.3.68 remain
necessary for final assembly. No terminal-configuration certificate is
used as a substitute for those arguments.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*,
combined manuscript (1 March 2004), printed pp.1151–1155.
-/
